<title>UK: LME copper weaker at end, nickel touches new low.</title>
<headline>LME copper weaker at end, nickel touches new low.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Ends afternoon kerb softer after breaching $2,150 support. Cash/threes backwardation little changed at $98/$100.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Also easier after failing to break above $1,570 resistance in morning.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Edges down to fresh 2-1/4 year low.</p>
<p>ZINC - Slightly firmer.</p>
<p>TIN/LEAD - Modest losses.</p>
</text>
